Z||000000||varnster||01-28-2001||12:07 AM||||just got a remote starter keyless entry at Sams club today for 48 bucks, took about 2 hours to install and it works great, hell it even comes with a instruction video that walks you through step by step. It even includes a 12v indicator and elec tape!there<BR>site is <A HREF="http://www.bulldogsecurity.com," TARGET=_blank>www.bulldogsecurity.com,</A>  if your<BR>looking for one take my word for it, this one<BR>has it all at a great price. The one I got is<BR>model rs112,HAVE TO BUY EXTRA RELAY FOR TRUNK||||reg||10
Z||000001||fropuff||01-28-2001||12:24 AM||||How does it work?  Starting the car I mean.  I was looking into getting one of those.  Is the remote one of those HUGE ones?  The ones that are about the size of a frickin Game Boy?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanks.  Good find!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000002||wkayl||01-28-2001||12:28 AM||||I had one put in by my cousin in Fargo ND over a year ago.  It will start the car from 2 to 3 blocks.  I love it.  I use the door lock and trunk release the most.  The starter part is just a fun toy to use.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/outline.jpg">   <BR>86GT original paint, interior, engine  <A HREF="http://www.fierowayne.homestead.com/fierowayne.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierowayne.homestead.com/fierowayne.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Elenor84||01-28-2001||03:33 AM||||Do u need to have power locks to have keyless entry?  or do u wire it with the kit?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sideview.jpg">  </A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||01-28-2001||05:50 AM||||You need to have power locks for the keyless entry to work.  Some kits come with power locks as an option.  Wish I could find a combination keyless entry/remote start/alarm system that would work with a manual tranny.  Most of the DIY kits I've seen are for auto trannys only.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||01-28-2001||08:04 AM||||Monkey, they don't make any remote start kits for manual tranny. But, if you are carefull to always use the parking brake, and always leave the car in neutral when you leave it, it is very easy to bypass the clutch start swtich.||||reg||1
Z||000006||cifc||01-28-2001||08:56 AM||||I had a remote start on my 5 sp Fiero.  I really wouldn't recommend it.  No matter how careful you are sooner or later you're gonna leave the car in gear, and the parking brake isn't gonna hold it.  <BR>However, on my Friends suburu we did come up with a method using reed switches that won't let the car start if it is in gear.  I've never tried it on the Fiero though.  I'll probably looki into this when I get an alarm for my new car.<BR>--Jason||||reg||1
Z||000007||varnster||01-28-2001||10:57 AM||||The unit prev discribed has a very small remote, just hardwire it in to your ignition<BR>wires, brake, doorlocks,domelight,and trunk<BR>using supplied relays, all wires are located<BR>under steering wheel. after taking out my driver seat the wires were easy to get to.you hook up about 12 wires.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||01-29-2001||12:22 PM||||I thought starting the car with the clutch out put too much stress on the starter...||||reg||
Z||000009||Monkeyman||01-29-2001||07:29 PM||||A local shop said that they could install an alarm/keyless entry/remote starter.  The only problem is the cost.  They want around $500 to do it.  I was thinking that I could do it much cheaper.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Phaeton||01-29-2001||11:06 PM||||Astrostart model 260M is made for manual transmissions.  All autostarts are a pain to put in for DIY's, the manual trannies just have a few more wires for the safety interlocks so it doesn't get started in gear.<P>The boss where I work gave all employees free autostarts because it was cheaper than having everybody plug in all winter.<BR>It took me five hours to install it right, it takes the regular techs about two or three hours but they want money to do it.<P>Bypassing the safeties to install an automatic remote start on a manual is a guarantee that eventually it WILL be started in gear at some point.  Pain and lawsuits!  Don't do it.||||reg||12
